========================================================
1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE
========================================================

Build a complete, functional, full-stack cybersecurity
application called "PrivacyGuard IPv6".

The project must monitor IPv6 local area network (LAN)
activity, detect suspicious network events, protect device
privacy using temporary pseudonyms and short-lived
authenticated sessions, and provide a modern security
monitoring dashboard.

The project must satisfy the following objectives:

1. Monitor IPv6 network activity.
2. Simulate five IPv6-enabled IoT devices.
3. Support rotating temporary IPv6 addresses.
4. Detect unauthorised Router Advertisement (RA) messages.
5. Detect abnormal Neighbour Discovery Protocol (NDP)
   message rates.
6. Implement short-lived authenticated monitoring sessions.
7. Generate temporary local device pseudonyms.
8. Automatically expire pseudonyms according to a
   configurable lifetime.
9. Prevent cross-tenant device correlation.
10. Calculate attack detection and false-positive metrics.
11. Display security alerts and analytics through a
    professional dashboard.
12. Provide reproducible automated tests and documented
    results.

IMPORTANT:
The initial version must work completely using software
simulation. No physical IoT devices or specialised hardware
must be required.

The application must not depend on paid APIs or cloud
services to run its core functionality.

Do not create only a UI prototype. Implement working
frontend components, backend APIs, detection logic, privacy
mechanisms, test scenarios, and persistent or appropriately
managed application state.

