14. ANALYTICS AND EVALUATION METRICS
========================================================

Create an evaluation service that calculates metrics
from actual labelled test events.

Implement:

A. TRUE POSITIVES (TP)
Attack cases correctly detected.

B. FALSE POSITIVES (FP)
Normal cases incorrectly flagged as attacks.

C. TRUE NEGATIVES (TN)
Normal cases correctly classified as normal.

D. FALSE NEGATIVES (FN)
Attack cases that were not detected.

E. DETECTION RATE / RECALL

Detection Rate = TP / (TP + FN) * 100

If the denominator is zero, return a safe, documented
result rather than dividing by zero.

F. FALSE-POSITIVE RATE

False-Positive Rate = FP / (FP + TN) * 100

Handle a zero denominator safely.

G. PRECISION

Precision = TP / (TP + FP) * 100

Handle a zero denominator safely.

H. F1 SCORE

F1 = 2 * Precision * Recall /
     (Precision + Recall)

Implement consistent handling of undefined cases.

I. PRIVACY METRICS

Calculate:
- Number of pseudonyms created
- Number of pseudonyms expired
- Number of rejected expired-pseudonym events
- Number of expired sessions rejected
- Number of cross-tenant access attempts rejected

Clearly distinguish attack-detection metrics from
privacy-control metrics.

Do not invent performance results.

If there are no completed test cases, show that the
metrics are unavailable or not yet measured.

